      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\), we start by taking the square root of both sides. This gives us two possible equations:\n\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n\\]\n\nWe will solve each equation separately.\n\n1. For \\(x - 5 = 3\\):\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3 \\implies x = 3 + 5 \\implies x = 8\n\\]\n\n2. For \\(x - 5 = -3\\):\n\\[\nx - 5 = -3 \\implies x = -3 + 5 \\implies x = 2\n\\]\n\nThe solutions to the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\). The roots of the equation are 8 and 2.\n\nTo find the sum of the roots, we add them together:\n\\[\n8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
