    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) and find the sum of the roots, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Solve the equation for \\(x\\)**:\n   \\[\n   (x - 5)^2 = 9\n   \\]\n   To eliminate the square, take the square root of both sides:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = \\pm 3\n   \\]\n   This gives us two separate equations to solve:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n   \\]\n   Solving these equations separately:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = 3 \\implies x = 3 + 5 \\implies x = 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = -3 \\implies x = -3 + 5 \\implies x = 2\n   \\]\n   So, the solutions to the equation are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\n2. **Identify the sum of the roots**:\n   The roots of the equation are \\(8\\) and \\(2\\). To find the sum of the roots, we add these values together:\n   \\[\n   8 + 2 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
